			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1779011437169,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "No -> 3 most common ICU causes:",
			"fontSize": 14,
			"fontFamily": 6,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "No -> 3 most common ICU causes:",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"rawText": ""
		},
		{
			"id": "s7_no_b",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 1516.3269759999998,
			"y": 1678.5159939999999,
			"width": 325.9024437057713,
			"height": 300,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 2,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 0,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "b0V",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 404872812,
			"version": 348,
			"versionNonce": 646304670,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1779011437170,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "1. Vit K deficiency (39.6%)\n   Low FVII, FX, Prot C, Prot S -> Poor nutrition, antibiotics,\nbiliary obstruction -> Rx: Vitamin K IV or PO; plasma\ngenerally avoidable\n\n2. Liver disease pattern (35.4%)\n    Low FV, low/normal fibrinogen, high FVIII -> Impaired\nhepatic synthesis -> In HF: correlates with TBili, GGT, IVC,\nTR severity -> Plasma NOT for routine INR correction in\nliver disease\n\n3. Occult DOAC effect (14.6%)\n   Anti-Xa DOAC on assay despite no reported\nanticoagulant use\n\nACLI: ~80-84% show >=50% drop in prothrombin activity\n(distinguishes from viral hepatitis)\n\nPersistent coagulopathy despite hemo optimization ->\nsuggests progression to cardiac cirrhosis",
			"fontSize": 12,
			"fontFamily": 6,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "1. Vit K deficiency (39.6%)\n   Low FVII, FX, Prot C, Prot S -> Poor nutrition, antibiotics, biliary obstruction -> Rx: Vitamin K IV or PO; plasma generally avoidable\n\n2. Liver disease pattern (35.4%)\n    Low FV, low/normal fibrinogen, high FVIII -> Impaired hepatic synthesis -> In HF: correlates with TBili, GGT, IVC, TR severity -> Plasma NOT for routine INR correction in liver disease\n\n3. Occult DOAC effect (14.6%)\n   Anti-Xa DOAC on assay despite no reported anticoagulant use\n\nACLI: ~80-84% show >=50% drop in prothrombin activity (distinguishes from viral hepatitis)\n\nPersistent coagulopathy despite hemo optimization -> suggests progression to cardiac cirrhosis",
			"autoResize": false,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"rawText": "1. Vit K deficiency (39.6%)\n   Low FVII, FX, Prot C, Prot S -> Poor nutrition, antibiotics, biliary obstruction -> Rx: Vitamin K IV or PO; plasma generally avoidable\n\n2. Liver disease pattern (35.4%)\n    Low FV, low/normal fibrinogen, high FVIII -> Impaired hepatic synthesis -> In HF: correlates with TBili, GGT, IVC, TR severity -> Plasma NOT for routine INR correction in liver disease\n\n3. Occult DOAC effect (14.6%)\n   Anti-Xa DOAC on assay despite no reported anticoagulant use\n\nACLI: ~80-84% show >=50% drop in prothrombin activity (distinguishes from viral hepatitis)\n\nPersistent coagulopathy despite hemo optimization -> suggests progression to cardiac cirrhosis",
			"link": null
		},
